1
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:10,740
Two clubs show how their members travel there, in pie charts.

2
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:14,320
In both charts, the cycle sector is 90 degrees.

3
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:18,070
Club A has 40 members, and club B has 200.

4
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:21,250
Do the same number of people cycle to each club?

5
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,440
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:24,690
No.

7
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:30,750
90 degrees is a quarter of the circle, so a quarter of each club cycles.

8
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,600
A quarter of 40 is 10.

9
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:35,080
A quarter of 200 is 50.

10
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:39,960
Remember: a sector's angle is its fraction of 360 degrees.

11
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:41,980
90 degrees is a quarter.

12
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:44,380
180 degrees is a half.

13
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:48,540
A pie chart shows proportions, which are fractions of the whole.

14
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,610
It does not show actual numbers.

15
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:54,800
Equal sectors can mean very different numbers of people.

16
00:00:54,850 --> 00:01:00,220
To find a number, use: the angle, divided by 360, times the total.

17
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:00,910
Your turn.

18
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,170
How many members of club B cycle?

19
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,360
Pause the video and check.

20
00:01:06,410 --> 00:01:09,430
90 divided by 360, times 200, is 50.

21
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:13,100
To compare proportions, compare the angles.

22
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:17,150
To compare numbers, work out each amount.

23
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,490
Here is the method.

24
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:19,550
Step 1: decide.

25
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:24,050
Is the question about a proportion, or an actual number?

26
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:28,990
Step 2: for proportions, compare the angles, or the fractions.

27
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:36,140
Step 3: for numbers, work out the angle divided by 360, times the total, for each chart.

28
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:40,430
Step 4: explain your conclusion, using both charts.

29
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:45,880
In school P, the Science sector is 108 degrees, out of 30 students.

30
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:49,940
In school Q, it is 96 degrees, out of 60 students.

31
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:53,850
Which has a greater proportion choosing Science?

32
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,080
108 is more than 96, so school P.

33
00:01:57,130 --> 00:02:01,370
But which has more students choosing Science?

34
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:04,410
P: 108 over 360, times 30, is 9.

35
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:07,460
Q: 96 over 360, times 60, is 16.

36
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:08,870
School Q.

37
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:09,680
Your turn.

38
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:12,780
How many is a 120 degree sector of 45?

39
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:15,970
Pause and work it out.

40
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:19,070
120 degrees is a third of 360.

41
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:21,680
A third of 45 is 15.

42
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:25,280
A sector of 60 degrees represents 15 people.

43
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:26,750
What is the total?

44
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,700
60 degrees is a sixth of the circle.

45
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:34,090
So the total is 15 times 6, which is 90 people.

46
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:38,140
In pie A, pasta is 180 degrees, out of 20 people.

47
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:42,180
In pie B, pasta is 120 degrees, out of 90 people.

48
00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:44,390
Which line is wrong?

49
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,670
Line 1 is wrong.

50
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:50,310
A bigger angle means a bigger proportion, not more people.

51
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,910
A: half of 20 is 10.

52
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,300
B: a third of 90 is 30.

53
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:56,860
More people like pasta in B.

54
00:02:56,910 --> 00:03:01,460
News reports often show pie charts of how a country spends its money.

55
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:04,730
Before comparing two countries, check the totals.

56
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:10,610
A small slice of a big budget can be more money than a big slice of a small one.

57
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:11,940
One last question.

58
00:03:11,990 --> 00:03:15,110
What is a 72 degree sector as a percentage?

59
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:18,500
Pause the video and answer.

60
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:23,750
72 divided by 360 is 0.2, which is 20 percent.

61
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:27,220
To remember: pie charts show proportions.

62
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:32,090
The number is the angle, divided by 360, times the total.

63
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:34,190
Compare proportions by angle.

64
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,980
Compare amounts by calculating.

65
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:39,990
Check the totals before you decide.

66
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:45,390
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.4 on Camday.
